 it's up to the operators  to do that but it would be a big mistake  to underestimate the value for the  existing cable infrastructure in the  last mile  while all this is going on what's your  view on the regulatory situation at the  moment it hasn't been that bad because  it's encouraged especially  infrastructure based competition and  cable our members are one of the main  driving force for high quality broadband  in Europe and our members benefit from  this infrastructure competition and in  areas where you have one hundred percent  cable coverage we have the best service  all over Europe so I sink infrastructure  competition is one key for get a quality  get better quality in broadband and when  competition works we could face out of  regulation this is already embedded in  the existing regulatory framework that  could be a little bit enhanced for  next-generation networks but you look  market by market but I think there is no  longer justification for regulation if  this infrastructure competition has so  fantastic results for the consumer yes  now you finish with the magic word the  consumer there sometimes we forget about  the consumer what do you think matters  most to them at the moment I think  consumers want to have a seamless  experience and they want to have a whole  bundle of different services at a very  reasonable price and that what cable  operators can offer you know we have  embedded Wi-Fi systems we have embedded  even content even high quality content  in a triple play bundle you know so it's  important not to sing only about  infrastructure it's important to think  about the services and what we see right  now is we are running ahead of the  demand you know so we would like the  politicians and the regulator and EU  commission to look more on the side of  the demand what can we do to stimulate  more the demand of new services and  that's a holistic view I think for a  digital Europe and we will deliver I'm  sure we will deliver the best  infrastructure broadband solution which  is technically feasible it's been  talking about the EU what what do you  think is the one single thing they could  do to help should have deliver on this  digital single market besides the demand  stimulation and besides thinking about  it I think the regulation which they do  should enable investment I think that's  a key issue because public money public  funding never can do the job  you know most of the money is coming  from private companies and from private  investors and they are very sensible on  changes in the regulatory framework so  what we should do is to look on these  private investors who by the way have  deliver the great job in the past it's  not that they have done nothing you know  they have delivered very good quality  and listen a little bit more what these  investors want and then in the end of  the day investors listen also on the  demand of the customers you know so if  you want to have a good business in a  competitive environment there is no way  that you have to listen to your customer  and to support the needs of the custom  so this is a healthy environment and I  think we should learn out of this  healthy environment and not distorting  it that's the main my main message to  the Commission sometimes thank you very  much for talking to us Thank You Brad
 

